# Test Driven Development Rules

- Use this rules only when the prompt specify to use it with the expression `Using TDD`
- Always write specs that describes and test the new feature to be implemented
- Always run the tests inside the corresponding container, backend container for rspec spec and frontend container for react testing specs
- When a test failS ALWAYS modify the tested code and never the spec
- Only modify a spec under these 3 conditions
  1. The test fails for a reason other than the tested code, in this case check the cause of the failure report it back and present a posible solution and wait for confirmation
  2. The implemententation of a new feature requires the spec to change in order to do a correct implementation
  3. The prompt explicityly requires to change the spec